3: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `a^.b^.c*` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component, and under `*` a key surviving before the star keeps the join nested under it. So make the level agree — if the `*` lands keyed, stop dissolving its siblings (drop a `^`, as in `x{a* b}`); if it lands keyless, dissolve the keys that survive on the others (a `^` per surviving level, as in `x{a* b^.c^.d*}`). Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
